  "body": "Found while fixing #3810. A plugin agent's Disconnect (`magpie <agent> default`, and now turning its plugin off or removing it) puts the keys back and takes out the one magpie added, but when the user's parent object was written inline, the file doesn't come back byte for byte.\n\nkilo.jsonc as the user had it:\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"model\": \"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5\",\n  \"provider\": { \"anthropic\": {} }\n}\n```\n\nConnected (`provider.magpie` is added into the inline object, which `internal/edit` expands), then disconnected: the `magpie` key is deleted, but `provider` comes back as\n\n```jsonc\n  \"provider\": {\n    \"anthropic\": {} }\n```\n\nThe values are the same; only whitespace differs. With the object written over several lines the file comes back byte for byte (what #3810's tests use, `TestPluginOffAndRemovePutTheAgentBack`).\n\nExpected: deleting a key `internal/edit` inserted into an inline object leaves the object as it was before the insert. Not changed in #3810's commit.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
