   "body": "Fixed on a fork branch: `fix/3814-inline-object-bytes` (head `6276ec7d`, on upstream `6eb510f7`) — an inline object keeps its line when magpie's entry comes and goes.\n\n**Root cause.** `internal/edit/json.go`'s `pretty` decided by the WHOLE FILE (`bytes.IndexByte(raw,'\\n') >= 0`), so an insert into a file whose target object is inline (`\"provider\": { \"anthropic\": {} }`) spread the object over lines, and no later read put the whitespace back.\n\n**Change.** the inline test is now about the target object's own span: it is inline when that span holds no newline, so an entry written into it and later removed round-trips byte for byte. A new file's placeholder keeps its pretty layout.\n\n**Verified.** Red: `go test -tags nogui ./internal/edit/ -run TestJSONInlineObjectRoundTrips` → `edit_test.go:144`: after set → provider spread over lines, the bytes differ from the original\nGreen: `same command → `ok`; `TestJSONInsertNestedIntoExistingObject` (multi-line) and `TestJSONCompact`/`TestDelJSONCompactAndComments` (single-line files) unchanged and green; package's tests pass but the pre-existing `TestWriteAtomicReadOnlyHardLink` (fails at base, umask)` → `ok github.com/yetone/magpie/internal/edit`\n\nFull `go test -tags nogui ./...` over round 27's branches: 70 packages ok, 5 red (edit `TestWriteAtomicReadOnlyHardLink`, gateway's five, plugin `TestPluginSOCKSProxy`, provider's synctest fatal in `TestUnreadLoginsWriteErrorsKeepCredentials`, testenv `TestProgram`) — every one of them reproduces identically at base `6eb510f7` in this environment (umask 0027), so none is from this change.\n\nBranch: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/3814-inline-object-bytes — no PR opened, this repo takes no external PRs; say the word if you'd rather have the patch inline here.",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
